      "status": "registered_query_snapshot_required",
      "basis": "USAspending revises continuously. The retrospective FY2025 fetch verifies the query shape and historical value but is not first-print evidence. A forecast target must define the outcome as the exact registered query response captured inside a preregistered post-fiscal-year snapshot window and archive the complete response bytes, following the existing USAspending adapter custody rule."
    },
    "adapterDisposition": {
      "family": "usaspending-api",
      "disposition": "extend_existing",
      "requiredWork": "Extend the existing fiscal_year_post_scalar registered-query builder to accept sealed awarding-subagency and placeOfPerformanceLocations transforms and emit the exact agencies and place_of_performance_locations filters above; add the series binding and parser tests while preserving the registered_query_snapshot release policy and complete raw-response custody. No new source family is required."
    },
    "parseNotes": [
      "The registered series identity must be exactly Forest Service as awarding subtier under Department of Agriculture plus place_of_performance_locations=[{country: USA, state: MN}]. The request filename and bill context must never be interpreted as a Superior National Forest filter.",
      "The FY2025 response reports 46,832,556.79 as 15,398,331.29 Contract_Obligations plus 21,158,670.82 Grant_Obligations plus 10,275,554.68 Other_Obligations; every other obligation bucket is zero and all outlay fields are null.",
      "Treat aggregated_amount as signed net award-transaction obligations and retain future deobligations. Do not relabel it as all Forest Service obligations, account spending, appropriations, budget authority, outlays, or bill-caused spending.",
      "Do not substitute the $2,241,795.07 keyword probe or a Cook/Lake/St. Louis county union for the registered Minnesota series. Neither identifies the Superior National Forest boundary.",
      "The local environment presented a self-signed TLS interception chain, so the successful live calls used curl --insecure against the exact official HTTPS URLs; every recorded hash and byte length is for the returned HTTP 200 response body bytes.",
      "The primary FY2025 response and its same-session replay are byte-identical at 1,150 bytes and SHA-256 685c55dd28dc9824d018ce6ebb960d612e3a1d66fb9beb77862b381b47282f20."
    ]
